WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.910
A neutral resx file
holds named strings,

2
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.067
and each translation is a copy
with the culture in its name.

3
00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:12.412
General Translation's CLI writes
those culture files from the

4
00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.479
neutral source.

5
00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.577
Translate only each value,

6
00:00:16.577 --> 00:00:18.400
and keep names, comments,

7
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.940
and placeholders such
as {0} unchanged.

8
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:29.407
Add a resx entry to gt.config.json
that puts the culture before

9
00:00:29.407 --> 00:00:30.323
the extension.

10
00:00:30.723 --> 00:00:35.344
Then npx gt translate writes the
French file beside the neutral

11
00:00:35.344 --> 00:00:35.726
one.

12
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.320
At run time, fr-CA falls back to fr,

13
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.758
then to the neutral file.

14
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.657
Your team now ships
French with each release.
